1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,033
A story is a wish for a better world. How do we split that wish?

2
00:00:05,033 --> 00:00:07,567
Three friends need to know what to pay.

3
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:12,033
Many teams split the solution: database, API, screen.

4
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:14,033
Those are parts of an answer.

5
00:00:14,033 --> 00:00:20,167
Problem decomposition splits customer problems: split equally; unequal shares; track payments.

6
00:00:20,167 --> 00:00:24,667
Two premises: seek smaller customer problems before choosing solutions.

7
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:27,533
A plan is an attempt, not a guarantee.

8
00:00:27,533 --> 00:00:30,933
Two goals. First: deliver value and feedback.

9
00:00:30,933 --> 00:00:34,900
One small story crosses the product. Now each friend knows what they owe.

10
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,000
Their reaction changes the next step.

11
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,400
Just enough, just in time to learn.

12
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:41,600
Second: make stopping affordable.

13
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:47,000
Completed value keeps working. Leave later stories unstarted, so you can change direction.

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:53,467
Four principles. Three Vs: valuable to customers, visible in their world, vertical through the product.

15
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:57,200
One-piece flow: finish one customer outcome together.

16
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,933
Repeat at smaller scales: stories, scenarios, implementation slices.

17
00:01:01,933 --> 00:01:04,167
Every commit is your last commit.

18
00:01:04,167 --> 00:01:12,600
Strive for useful value now; serve today's purpose or an already documented need, including product health, not merely prepare the next commit.

19
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,333
Care for the whole product. Assimilate each splash into a coherent design.

20
00:01:17,333 --> 00:01:21,467
Healthy design preserves speculative future potential: option value.

21
00:01:21,467 --> 00:01:24,900
Unused features can add complexity and close alternatives.

22
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:30,667
Smaller problems. Useful impacts. Freedom to choose again.
